## Negative control — the ORIGINAL M-1 red mechanism reproduced at production serving
An undici/browser fetch POST with a JSON string body and NO explicit content-type sends `content-type: text/plain;charset=UTF-8`. Reproduced verbatim against PRODUCTION-served Quellight:
POST http://localhost:4742/api/act
  content-type: text/plain;charset=UTF-8   <-- header-less fetch default
HTTP:403
Body: "Cross-site POST form submissions are forbidden"   (SvelteKit production CSRF guard)

## Positive control (same body, content-type: application/json), production serving
HTTP:200

## Dev-mode note (matches the original audit's empirical matrix)
The identical no-content-type POST against the DEV server (:4739) returns 200 — dev mode does not run the CSRF guard; this is exactly how the original accepted evidence was masked.

